abstract: >-
  TapeLM (variant A) couples a dual-channel character-curve encoder pretrained once (Stage 191)
  and frozen for product memory use with zero-training-at-inference fingerprint modules—lexicon
  calibration, episodic slots, subject writes, and hop/bind composition—in the same normalized
  fp-space as next-token generation. Extensions 221–230 add canonical slot storage, offline-fit
  family W for domain qmap, fp decode (228c), and contradiction resolution (230) without
  finetuning P1 on fact ingest. Product shipping trunk: 221 -> 227 -> 228c -> 230 -> 226c. The artifact documents matched-GPT parity, fp capability wins
  (calibration, recall, edit, stream, hops), honest fair GPT+RAG comparisons, capability wins on
  noisy/OOV text and slot unlearn, explicit limits (generative fingerprints, hybrid rerankers,
  internalization Stages 210–212), and cross-domain utilization via fp decode (226c).
